# Opt-in fragment (T71), merged by cmd/thunder only when the Nimbusfile
# declares `AGENT vmware` (mirrors vga.fragment/CNIMBUS_VGA's own
# opt-in pattern exactly). amd64-only: VMware's I/O-port backdoor is an
# x86 mechanism with no arm64 equivalent.
#
# iopl(2)/ioperm(2): the AGENT vmware kind (cmd/cnimbusagent) needs
# ring-3 IN/OUT access to poke VMware's backdoor I/O port (0x5658) --
# gated behind this symbol since kernel 5.5 (previously always compiled
# in). Without it, iopl(2) fails with ENOSYS and AGENT vmware can never
# succeed, even under real VMware (verified empirically -- this is
# exactly what broke it before this symbol was first added). Previously
# always merged into every amd64 image via vm-amd64.fragment regardless
# of whether AGENT vmware was ever declared; moved here so it's a
# declared capability rather than an ambient one granted to every image.
CONFIG_X86_IOPL_IOPERM=y
